WEBVTT

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:08.610
<i>For the first time, I realized</i>

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:11.740
<i>that the special emotion of love
could be such a burden.</i>

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.950
<i>Unlike a performance, I can't control myself.</i>

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.740
<i>Even as that left me at a loss,</i>

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:22.540
<i>I was being remade
from the inside out, body and soul.</i>

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:28.090
<i>The proof of that is even in the middle
of this huge crowd, I bet I can find you.</i>

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.670
<i>See? There you are.</i>

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.510
<i>Jeez, give me a break already.</i>

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:15.650
hug 10 "We're breaking up, Chunta."

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:17.820
You look pathetic, Ayagi!

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:17.110
PROGRAMS 2300 YEN

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.450
That's awesome, Chihi!

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.870
Why do I have to do this?!

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.250
The rule is whoever makes
the most mistakes that day

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:28.410
has to stay in costume afterwards
and sell programs.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:31.460
Who fumbled his words in the first act again?

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.170
Yes, yes, it was me!

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:34.590
I'm sorry!

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.720
Why did it have to be
during the last performance?

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.260
I must have been too enthusiastic
since it was the last one.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.930
This isn't like me!

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:45.850
At least it shows
that you were taking it seriously.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:48.270
Not bad.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:50.520
For a stage debut, you pass.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.350
Good job, leading actor.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:56.780
I'm serious after all.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.860
Mr. Saijo, I've seriously fallen in love...

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.700
- Ow! Ow! Ow! That hurts!
- Ayagi, you were great out there!

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.950
In your scenes with Takato,

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:09.080
you made me want to jump onto the stage
and run through you with a sword.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.370
Is that right?

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.880
Thanks for not stabbing me with a sword.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:17.380
"THE RED LEAF OGRE"
TAKATO SAIJO

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.380
Well, I guess I'll change.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.590
Wait! What are you doing following me in?!

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:21.430
Get out!

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:26.260
I already told Mr. Sasaki
that I'll take care of you afterwards, so...

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.310
Mr. Sasaki.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:33.440
Besides, I wanted to see you
in that outfit to the very end.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:37.230
You really are amazing, Takato.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.440
I find myself gazing at your every movement.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:44.070
It would be a waste
to miss even a single moment.

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:48.450
Well, when you've got my talent,
it's easier than it looks.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.000
Are you filled with awe?

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:50.830
Yes.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:55.080
You've enchanted me, Takato Saijo.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:58.670
You truly show me a radiant sight.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:01.800
<i>This guy.</i>

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:07.100
<i>When he talks to me like that,
I can't tell whether I'm happy or embarrassed.</i>

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.310
You can stop sucking up to me now.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:11.310
Just get out of here.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:13.480
I'm not sucking up to you!

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:14.350
What?!

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:17.820
I was jealous of Ayagi
for getting to co-star with you.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.690
If I could've gotten away with it,

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:22.950
I really would have run through him
with a sword and then taken over his role.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:24.780
<i>What is this?</i>

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.660
<i>I'm as red as a beet.</i>

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.790
Takato, do you remember our agreement?

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.500
About "no touching" until the play was over?

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.870
Yeah, but this is my dressing room.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.460
And there's a cast party.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.590
<i>His hands are hot.</i>

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:41.800
Good point.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:44.050
You're still working until the cast party is over.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:46.680
<i>How badly is he holding back?</i>

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:50.390
<i>Is he the only one holding back?</i>

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:52.930
A little...

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:55.810
A little bit would be okay.

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:59.150
A quick kiss or like that would be fine.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:08.410
You!

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.660
I said only a kiss!

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:13.080
You saying it's okay to kiss you...

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:16.170
I've been holding back all this time,
so that's like poison to me!

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:17.420
The door.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:19.290
Lock the door!

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:24.010
That's right. Somebody could just walk in.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:24.920
Idiot!

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:27.090
L-Lock it, Chunta!

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:29.220
Look, Takato.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:33.100
Do you see the expression on your face?

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:37.730
<i>Who is that?</i>

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:39.480
<i>Me?</i>

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:42.730
N-No! It's not!

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:46.360
Takato, if you want me, look in the mirror.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:49.070
Unless you don't want any more than this?

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:50.950
<i>I want more.</i>

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.700
<i>I want to feel him more.</i>

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:54.790
<i>But...</i>

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:57.000
<i>This disgraceful face...</i>

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:58.330
<i>I hate it.</i>

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:00.880
You saw it, didn't you?

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:04.380
Your melted face is beautiful, Takato.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:06.590
Mr. Saijo,

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:08.340
- if you're ready...
- Chunta, th-the door!

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:09.930
- how about going with us to the restaurant?
- It's okay.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:11.050
Moron, it's not okay!

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:13.060
It's fine, I tell you.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:15.640
Wait a second. Look.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:18.770
Sorry!

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:21.480
Oh, no, I totally didn't notice!

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.360
You have to pay attention to these things.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.730
There. Cry out, Takato.

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:26.570
No.

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:29.990
TAKING A NAP FOR HALF AN HOUR.
PLEASE DON'T WAKE ME.

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:34.030
You even put a sign up...

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:37.290
and locked the door when you came in.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.080
Pay me back for shortening my life span!

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.000
You incorrigible, insatiable angel!

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.250
I'm sorry.

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:46.550
But you were so adorable, Takato!

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:49.760
- Hello?
- Hello?

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.930
- Oh, Mr. Taguchi?
- Oh, Mr. Sasaki?

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:55.430
Really?

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:56.720
- Yes.
- Okay.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:06:58.810
Chunta.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:06:59.980
Takato.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:03.650
Apparently they're going to do
a sequel to "Midday Star."

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:06.320
<i>So that means...</i>

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:08.570
<i>I'll be with him again.</i>

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:11.610
Takato!

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:15.370
I'm overjoyed and excited!

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:16.830
Can I kiss you?!

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:23.130
MR. TAGUCHI
CALL END

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.330
Enough! You pest!

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.120
Don't be bashful!

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.130
I'm not bashful!

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:37.220
When I was still a showbiz kid,
Mr. Nakata taught me something.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:40.770
He said you could tell when someone
was about to get ahead by their shoes.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:45.900
Did you buy the latest model
on a business trip abroad, Mr. Usaka?

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.440
You need to watch your step, or you'll fail.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:52.280
You'd better keep your feet
planted firmly too, Takato.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:56.950
I heard you're going to be
in charge of the sequel.

00:07:56.950 --> 00:08:00.580
Were you that fond of "Midday Star"?

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:06.210
Yes. The cast, the director, the crew,
the publicity, there was nothing to be desired.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:10.170
However, if I had been in charge,
it would have been even better.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:13.090
You're as confident as ever.

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:16.720
I plan to make the sequel flawless.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:18.720
The only thing,
this took a bit of wind out of my sails.

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:20.890
WEEKLY TOBUN

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:20.890
The Tobun, huh?

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:22.600
Did they pull a gotcha?

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:26.230
They did. The photo of an actress
I was going to use kissing a guy in the street.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:28.400
Talented paparazzi.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:31.190
He made it look like a slightly erotic kiss.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:33.320
Now I can't use her.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:37.160
I'll have to choose someone else.
If someone is even a slight risk, they're gone.

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:39.410
You wouldn't be immune, Takato.

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:40.540
I know.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:45.250
That reminds me. It seems you've been really
chummy with your co-star, Junta Azumaya.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:49.460
The annoying angelic guy
with the aura and flapping wings?

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:51.090
Not at all! We're not close at all!

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:53.760
I don't know what you're babbling about,

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:56.180
but it's unusual for you
to hang out with a fellow actor.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:59.560
We don't, really.
He's just become attached to me.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:08.270
You think I would let the merchandise
breathe secondhand smoke?

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:10.320
Tch. No, I didn't think so.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:11.530
You clicked your tongue.

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.190
Oh, you heard that?

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:16.490
Well, I just stopped by to say hi,
so I'll be on my way.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:20.620
Feel free to inhale tar
until your lungs are as black as your heart.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:22.580
Takato.

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:25.120
I never fight a losing battle.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:28.290
You're telling me that?

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:38.840
<i>I always think of him as a kid,
but then he turns on the charm.</i>

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:42.970
<i>Dangerous.</i>

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.560
Jun!

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:49.400
I heard about the sequel to "Midday Star"!
Congratulations!

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:50.940
Thank you.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:54.360
- Your knees! Your knees are so cute!
- Boss, I told you before not to touch Azumaya!

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:55.490
You'll taint him!

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:59.320
Just this once,
I feel grateful for that louse, Takato.

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:03.410
I never thought the day would come,
not after Takato almost put us out of business.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:05.410
Don't remind me!

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:11.460
How many of our agency's handsome devils
were overshadowed by Takato?

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:17.800
But just when we were drowning
in an ocean of tears, our savior appeared!

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.350
Sorry for the wait. Your Doremi Pizza is here!

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:25.890
A diamond in the rough!

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:27.310
Boss! Calm down!

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:29.310
- Just as you ordered, Basil Deluxe
- An exceptional diamond in the rough

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:30.980
- and a Garlic Pepper Doremi Special.
- has come bearing pizza!

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:32.860
- I don't need pizza!
- Boss! Our find will run away!

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.280
- Please be careful, because it's very hot.
- What's your name, kid?

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:40.610
But that very same Takato boosted our Jun
to the next stage of his career.

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:42.120
So it balances out.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:47.080
That's because Azumaya improved a lot
after co-starring with Takato.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:48.330
Thank you.

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:51.750
That's right. You've changed, Jun.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.710
Which is why I'm a bit worried.

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:57.090
You heard about the girl
who was slated to appear in the sequel

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:59.300
but got the axe
after a candid photo was published?

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:03.390
Well, there's no danger of Azumaya
being caught in similar circumstances!

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:05.060
I know.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:08.180
But it's better to err on the side of caution, Jun.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:09.440
Right.

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:12.610
Of course, I'm always open to having
a scandalous relationship with you!

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:15.980
I told you not to sexually harass him!

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:18.900
Oh, shut up! Jun is my angel!

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:20.320
There are limits to everything!

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:22.360
WEEKLY TOBUN

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:22.360
Please contain yourself!

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:30.960
Did you plant a GPS on me?

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.920
I wouldn't cut corners like that with you, Takato.

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:35.000
That's even scarier!

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.380
If you don't cut corners, how do you do it?!

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:39.050
Mr. Sasaki?! It's Mr. Sasaki, isn't it?!

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:41.630
You've bribed my manager.

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:42.840
Takato, watch your—

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:43.720
Takato!

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:55.230
S-Sorry.

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:56.770
What's wrong?

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:57.900
Nothing.

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.900
It's nothing. Let's go.

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:08.290
That was close.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:11.210
Is it normal to sense my presence
from that distance?

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:14.290
But those two again.

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:19.880
I can't believe it, but what if, what if...
It could possibly be.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.130
Probably not.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:26.800
Would it be worth staking them out?

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:34.020
What is it, Takato?

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:35.060
Nothing.

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:37.690
Let's go. I want to get home and have a drink.

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:45.450
<i>Chunta has been acting strange
the past few days.</i>

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:47.620
<i>He isn't as clingy as usual.</i>

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:55.960
They've suddenly
stopped messing around outside,

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.920
so I'll just have to take a peek inside.

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:04.180
<i>In order to bypass security,
I had to resort to old tricks,</i>

00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:06.090
<i>using time and my body to obtain a key card.</i>

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:10.220
You two owe me a good photo.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:14.230
Takato, are you in a bad mood?

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:16.230
I'm fine.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:17.650
Then do you feel under the weather?

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:19.020
I'm fine.

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:21.900
<i>Should I tell him the truth?</i>

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:24.150
<i>I don't know how to bring it up.</i>

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:27.160
<i>The way this is going,
never mind about being lov... roommates.</i>

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:33.040
Takato, shall we go in?

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:34.620
Chunta!

00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:37.420
I, um...

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:40.590
<i>Somehow...
Somehow I have to show my feelings.</i>

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:42.250
Uh...

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:55.350
Where did that come from?!

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:59.060
Takato, you won't let me hold back, will you?

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:03.780
Once we get in the apartment,
we can continue, right?

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:06.400
Wh-Why even bother asking?
You're going to do it either way.

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:10.120
<i>I answered him again like that.</i>

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:15.330
Bingo.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:19.920
"MIDDAY STAR"

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:22.840
<i>Co-stars.</i>

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.800
<i>He's improved so much.</i>

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:33.850
<i>He did a great job playing a complex character
in that drama, "Witch's Drip."</i>

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.020
<i>So much that he even held his own</i>

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:39.140
<i>against the intense performance
of veteran actress Yurie Kurokawa.</i>

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:43.270
<i>How much further will he grow as an actor?</i>

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:48.070
<i>Even as I'm afraid
of his seemingly bottomless talent,</i>

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:52.070
<i>I want to give him a supportive push.</i>

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:55.790
Am I getting too soft?

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:58.910
<i>No good. No good. My policy
is to hammer the nail that sticks out.</i>

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:02.420
All right, so how can I wipe the floor with him?

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:06.550
This'll be a competition between me and Chunta
to see which of us can catch the audience's eye.

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:10.090
I can't wait to see him cry when I win.

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:12.300
"MIDDAY STAR"

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:14.850
I forgot about this.

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:18.480
Takato.

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:21.020
Let me drop you off at your place.

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:23.860
No, that's okay.
You start in the afternoon, don't you?

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:25.980
You'd better prepare.

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:27.150
Okay.

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:29.900
Then take this with you.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:31.110
What is it?

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:32.910
Info on apartments.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:38.000
Just so you know,
I'm not moving out of Naka-Meguro.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:40.660
I know. All of the potential
apartments in there are in Naka-Meguro.

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:43.920
And I want the bathroom to have a window,
and I want a big balcony.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:44.750
Sure.

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:45.840
Of course, it'll have to face south.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:46.630
Takato.

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:52.760
That was my "see you later" kiss.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:55.300
Once we're living together,
we can do this every day.

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:57.180
You...

00:15:57.390 --> 00:15:59.680
I'm not so cheap
to let you do that every single day!

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:00.560
Get lost, dummy!

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:02.230
Idiot! Stupid angel!

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:07.150
I'll save up a lot of 1,000-yen bills
until we move in together.

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:11.700
So don't turn your face away from me so much.

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:17.410
Don't turn my face away?

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:19.870
That's your fault!

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:21.210
Damn it!

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:24.880
Why do I have to be so fidgety?

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:28.460
In the first place, I'm supposed to be
the cool, calm, collected type!

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:31.050
But because of him, that... that...

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:32.170
Ow!

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:33.340
I hit my ankle!

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:36.720
Jeez! Who is this?!

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:38.390
Mr. Sasaki.

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:40.850
Yes. Yes.

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:48.690
I never thought you would be involved
in something like this.

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:50.400
Well...

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:52.070
The "Weekly Tobun" comes out tomorrow.

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:55.410
No matter what we do now,
we can't stop it from being published.

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:58.830
This is going to cause a stir.

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:58.830
SCOOP

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:10.090
Saijo. I'm going to have to take you
off the picture.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:13.920
I'm eliminating any risk.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:17.010
Saijo, I told you that would apply to you, too.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:18.760
Right.

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:20.470
I apologize.

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:21.430
Mr. Usaka, please w—

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:22.430
Please wait!

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:25.520
Azumaya, you can't just barge in there!

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:26.900
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:28.110
- We're leaving right now!
- Chunta.

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:30.320
I'm the other person in the photo.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:38.530
WEEKLY TOBUN

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:32.320
So I've heard.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:36.740
This is just a photo of me supporting Mr. Saijo
when he lost his footing on the stairs!

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:38.530
There's no sense making a fuss about it!

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:41.870
The public will decide
whether there's a fuss to be made or not.

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:45.660
Then if there is a fuss about it,
I'm responsible, too.

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:47.000
If you're cutting Mr. Saijo from the movie...

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:49.710
If I cut him, what will you do about it?

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:53.170
Are you telling me
that even though you're the lead,

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:55.170
you'll quit unless Takato Saijo is your co-star?

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:06.140
That's not what I'm saying.

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:11.320
I see. Then be very careful
about not feeding tasty tidbits to the media.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:14.490
I'll be in touch about the rest.

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:15.320
- Y-Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:19.370
Mr. Usaka, I apologize for the trouble.

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:24.330
Takato, maybe you should think
about your future course.

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:26.830
For your sake and his.

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:36.010
Well, shall we go our separate ways?

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:37.420
R-Right.

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:42.010
I'm going back to the office,
but you should go home and relax, Takato.

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:42.890
You must be exhausted.

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:45.600
Sorry. Excuse me.

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:48.350
Takato!

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:53.230
Cool off a bit.

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:55.480
Think about yourself.

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:11.000
A handsome man makes a good picture
even when he's troubled.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:13.670
Are you the one who took that photo?

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:15.920
- Yeah.
- You're talented.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:18.420
You made it look
like something romantic was happening.

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:20.090
You're wasting your talent, though.

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:22.390
That photo wasn't tabloid-worthy.

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:24.100
In the end, it's a hoax.

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:29.940
Even without a definitive photo, people
enjoy looking at things in an amusing way.

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:35.730
A photo like that isn't even worth
the time it takes those "people" to look at it.

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:38.780
Then how about a photo like this?

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:43.530
Go ahead. Tear it up.

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:45.240
I've got the data.

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:46.830
Why?

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:48.700
It's a good photo, isn't it?

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:51.960
It's so good that I haven't even
sold it to the magazine yet.

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:54.880
Damn it! So why did you show it to me?!

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:56.210
To make a deal.

00:19:56.880 --> 00:20:02.640
If you help me take an even better photo,
this one will never go to a publisher.

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:05.300
I'll let you make the decision.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.100
Think about it.

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:15.230
"VIAL OF THE SUN"

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:17.440
CHUNTA

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:23.200
<i>Not yet.</i>

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:25.320
<i>I can't let it end like this!</i>

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:26.660
<i>Then...</i>

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:30.540
<i>I'll end it for you.</i>

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.880
<i>What a smart-aleck.</i>

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:43.510
<i>Not many actors have
this kind of overbearing magnetism.</i>

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:45.930
<i>There's nothing you can do
to turn off the charm.</i>

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:49.140
<i>That talent is a treasure.</i>

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:53.940
Well, I guess it can't be helped.

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:06.200
Takato!

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:08.660
Sorry for calling you over here.

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:11.250
No problem.

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:14.790
You remembered this place, Takato.

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:15.710
I guess I did.

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:21.340
You told me that gazing at these factories
at night help you calm down,

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:22.920
and you were right.

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:26.760
When I look at those clear lights,
I can face myself.

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:28.390
It's a good place.

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:31.930
I've made a lot of decisions here.

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:36.270
About work and my feelings for you, too.

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:39.980
I've made a decision too.

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:51.240
We're breaking up, Chunta.

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:27.720
What the hell are you hiding from me?

00:23:27.720 --> 00:23:29.630
I'm just breaking up. That's all.

00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:30.590
There's nothing behind it.

00:23:30.590 --> 00:23:31.550
Liar.

00:23:31.550 --> 00:23:32.850
It's not a lie.

00:23:34.430 --> 00:23:40.020
hug 11
"If you're that in love with me, you can
have your way with me until you're done."
